 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Our CTO just forwarded me an email from procurement asking 'what happens if we need to leave Google' for the claims-triage agent we built on ADK + Vertex AI + Agent Engine. I don't want to touch the code right now, we ship to UAT in 3 weeks. Can you look through the repo and write me a doc on how painful it'd be to move to AWS (Bedrock/Lambda probably) or Azure, and what we'd have to rip out if we dropped ADK for LangGraph or something? Need risks, which bits we should keep behind an interface, and a phased plan with rough effort sizing (S/M/L is fine). Needs to be readable by non-engineers."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "vendor lock-in assessment for the agent in /services/support_agent. ADK on Cloud Run, Firestore sessions, Gemini 2.5, BigQuery tools. no code changes, just a markdown report: portability to aws/azure, swapping the framework, risk table, staged migration w/ relative effort. go."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "ok so we've decided — leadership wants the ADK agent running on Azure by end of Q1. Can you start rewriting our session service so it uses Cosmos DB instead of Firestore, and swap the Vertex model calls for Azure OpenAI? The tests in tests/test_sessions.py should still pass afterwards. Ugh, this is the third time this year the plan changed.", "needs_instead": "Actual migration implementation work: changing code to replace the Firestore session backend with Cosmos DB and Vertex model calls with Azure OpenAI, and keeping tests passing — not a written lock-in assessment without changing the build."}
